{"nodes": [{"id": "test_eventstream_streamequivalence_test_streaming_gates", "label": "streamEquivalence.test.js (7-gate formal streaming test file, 110 tests)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".superpowers/sdd/task-K6-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_superpowers_sdd_task_k6_report_fffe_endianness_regression", "label": "FFFE item-tag endianness regression (getU16LE/getU32LE false fix, reverted)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".superpowers/sdd/task-K6-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "K6 initially forced little-endian reads of FFFE-family tags citing a false PS3.5 \u00a77.5 claim; the real cause was a malformed EBE test fixture writing item tags in LE. Buffered fromPart10 honors body endianness via Tag.readTag; the LE-forced helpers were removed, the fixture rebuilt with BE item tags, and Gate 3 became a real oracle test."}, {"id": "_superpowers_sdd_task_k6_report_bounded_memory_gate", "label": "Bounded-memory gate (peak retained bytes < fragment + chunk + slack, paced feed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".superpowers/sdd/task-K6-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The feed must be paced by the listener's drain \u2014 an unpaced feed measures nothing. Encapsulated bound: 262144+65536+16384=344064 bytes; observed peak ~328KB, final retention 0."}, {"id": "_superpowers_sdd_task_k6_report_backpressure_gate", "label": "Backpressure gate (promise-driven drain blocking, no element N+2 while blocked)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".superpowers/sdd/task-K6-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "drainBlocker must be installed BEFORE fromPart10Stream is called: with ArrayBuffer